{:edb/db-before-t 1390 :edb/db-after-t 1391 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534703 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:37:11.745Z" 13194139534703 true] [17592186064229 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304404 13194139534703 true] [17592186064230 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304387 13194139534703 true] [17592186064230 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304390 13194139534703 true] [17592186064230 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304397 13194139534703 true] [17592186064804 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534703 true] [17592186064804 1100 "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ below have a discontinuity at $x =-1$?\n$f(x) = {x^{3} + x,\\begin{vmatrix}x < - 1 \\\\ x^{2} + 1,\\end{vmatrix}x \\ge - 1$" 13194139534703 false] [17592186064804 1100 "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ below have a discontinuity at $x=-1?$ \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+x, & x<-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1, & x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186064804 1145 "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- $f(-1)=(-1)^{2}+1=2,$ so $f(-1)$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and check if they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}({x}^{3}+x) \\\\  & =(-1)^{3}+(-1) \\\\  & =-2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the one-sided limits exist but are not equal. $\\,\\,\\times $ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-1$ because ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x).$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304387 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304388 13194139534703 true] [17592186304387 1089 "q-342242" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304387 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534703 true] [17592186304387 1100 "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=6$ and $f(6)=14,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {6}^{+}}\\sqrt{f(x)+{x}^{2}-1}=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534703 true] [17592186304387 1113 #uuid "b0898607-40ba-5160-b291-bbfc5674ac89" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304387 1145 "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=6.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to 6}f(x)$ exists and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {6}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to 6}f(x)=f(6)=14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {6}^{+}}\\sqrt{f(x)+{x}^{2}-1} & =\\sqrt{14+{6}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304388 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304389 13194139534703 true] [17592186304388 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534703 true] [17592186304388 1041 "field-1" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304388 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304389 13194139534703 true] [17592186304388 1110 #uuid "29f42fa8-490c-526d-b6af-3979ac2774c0" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304389 1034 "7" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304389 1111 #uuid "76210bf0-b3ae-5675-aa60-65ed8fba1577" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304390 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304391 13194139534703 true] [17592186304390 1089 "q-71068" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304390 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534703 true] [17592186304390 1100 "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)=8,$ then what is the value of $\\sqrt{f(-1)+1}?$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304390 1113 #uuid "22f74da2-9345-55bb-831c-5f5f24cacef0" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304390 1145 "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)$ exists, and\n\n$$\nf(-1)={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)=8.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{f(-1)+1} & =\\sqrt{8+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304392 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304393 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304394 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304395 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304396 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1041 "selection" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304395 13194139534703 true] [17592186304391 1110 #uuid "f6edc00b-3d38-589c-898c-269b98486106" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304392 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304392 1111 #uuid "676972b0-9c38-555e-aa6c-98b2576391e4" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304393 1034 "9" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304393 1111 #uuid "71a6bb71-4604-51f2-8c37-2d5b05a0a08e" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304394 1034 "\\sqrt{10}" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304394 1111 #uuid "7b9e4522-c31d-5a7f-bac7-b6645a714993" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304395 1034 "3" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304395 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304395 1111 #uuid "8450d8cf-2a55-5c0b-b6ca-41a99c6809a2" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304396 1034 "2\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304396 1111 #uuid "8e63c9f9-177f-5b35-8632-17b0012d74b3" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304397 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304398 13194139534703 true] [17592186304397 1089 "q-71071" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304397 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534703 true] [17592186304397 1100 "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4$ and $f(4)=2,$ then what is ${lim}_{x\\to 4}{({x}^{2}-6f(x))}^{2}?$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304397 1113 #uuid "eeea373f-95bb-5842-a9f9-990d433fa820" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304397 1145 "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to 4}f(x)$ exists, and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 4}f(x)=f(4)=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}{({x}^{2}-6f(x))}^{2} & ={({4}^{2}-6(2))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(16-12)}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304399 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304400 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304401 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304402 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304403 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1041 "selection" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304400 13194139534703 true] [17592186304398 1110 #uuid "6ac9bc9e-08a9-59ce-9726-fe81c86b198c" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304399 1034 "9" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304399 1111 #uuid "d55ffa54-16ff-5309-9227-f9eddcec0dd4" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304400 1034 "16" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304400 1111 #uuid "92725a5b-0cb3-5c0a-b256-4d7c8498acb8" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304401 1034 "36" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304401 1111 #uuid "a4ea99a2-5320-550c-b408-59fb4d23af63" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304402 1034 "25" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304402 1111 #uuid "d58972ba-c40c-53b6-bc5e-7b0121468430" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304403 1034 "4" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534703 true] [17592186304403 1111 #uuid "5af31e22-830a-53c3-8f12-4cacbb72a828" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304404 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304405 13194139534703 true] [17592186304404 1089 "q-71080" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304404 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534703 true] [17592186304404 1100 "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ given below have a discontinuity at $x=2?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-2x+3, & x<2 \\\\ 2x-3, & x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304404 1113 #uuid "a5fc9af3-149c-5207-9936-917f743c751e" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304404 1145 "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- $f(2)=2(2)-3=1,$ so $f(2)$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and check if they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(-2x+3) \\\\  & =-2(2)+3 \\\\  & =-1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(2x-3) \\\\  & =2(2)-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the one-sided limits exist but are not equal. Therefore, ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist. $\\times $ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$ because ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist." 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304406 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304407 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304408 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304409 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304410 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1041 "selection" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304406 13194139534703 true] [17592186304405 1110 #uuid "f0bde795-7c9d-5fcf-adaa-aa6a537785b7" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304406 1034 "${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534703 true] [17592186304406 1111 #uuid "a211603e-ede9-52c2-a8e1-d000c64df542" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304407 1034 "$f(2)$ does not exist" 13194139534703 true] [17592186304407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534703 true] [17592186304407 1111 #uuid "8401d42d-29e4-51cb-be08-d69ea97c9132" 13194139534703 true] [1759218630